<title>UK: UK new car sales dip 0.23 pct in March -- SMMT.</title>
<headline>UK new car sales dip 0.23 pct in March -- SMMT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British new car sales</p>
<p> March		     179,863 vs 180,275 -- down 0.23 pct</p>
<p> Year to date	    549,534 vs 531,049 -- up 3.48 pct</p>
<p>Total for month by marque, market share in pct vs year ago  Ford		30,462 (16.9 pct) vs  35,534 (19.7 pct)</p>
<p> General Motors 24,201 (13.5 pct) vs  28,006 (15.5 pct)</p>
<p> Rover Group  19,674 (10.9 pct) vs  21,534 (12.0 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot     13,061  (7.3 pct) vs  13,820  (7.7 pct)</p>
<p> Renault     12,113  (6.7 pct) vs  11,017  (6.1 pct)</p>
<p> VW		9,276  (5.2 pct) vs   8,650  (4.8 pct)</p>
<p> Citroen	9,787  (5.4 pct) vs   5,879  (3.3 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan	  8,066  (4.5 pct) vs   8,580  (4.8 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat	    8,329  (4.6 pct) vs   6,556  (3.6 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota	  6,141  (3.4 pct) vs   5,019  (2.8 pct)</p>
<p>Total yr to date by marque, market share in pct vs year ago</p>
<p> Ford		97,666 (17.8 pct) vs 110,935 (20.9 pct)</p>
